   "reason": "[\"The exception clause ('except as said applicants may be affected by the stay of the code granted by the Administrator's order of July 30, 1933, pending my final determination ...') ends before the June 14, 1935 repeal, and the ending records are not evidence in this packet. Held but not packet evidence: jobs/app-executive-orders/output/texts/executive-order-6476-terminating-stay-provisions-the-cotton-textile-industry-code.txt (EO 6476, December 4, 1933: stay terminated and provisions in full force 'from and after December 11, 1933'), executive-order-6407-terminating-stay-the-provisions-the-cotton-textile-industry-code.txt (EO 6407, November 6, 1933) and executive-order-6463-extension-stay-the-provision-the-cotton-textile-code.txt (EO 6463, November 27, 1933), with HathiTrust GPO copies jobs/hathi-gpo-orders/output/texts/EO_6407.txt, EO_6463.txt and EO_6476.txt. The kit cites only dossier evidence records and the machine found no actor provision linking these orders to EO 6242-C (they recite 'the Administrator's order of July 30, 1933' and 'Executive orders issued by me November 6, 1933' without numbers). Needed: re-prepare the packet with source-supplement excerpts of EO 6407, 6463 and 6476 (with their page checks) as end evidence, then submit two clauses (the denial exhausted 1933-08-04 and the exception ended about 1933-12-11) with the shared repeal as a later event on the denial.\", \"The machine inventory is one whole clause (characters 535-1850) that merges the denial and the exception; the corrected inventory (denial: 'do order that the application ... be and it is hereby denied'; exception: 'except as said applicants may be affected by the stay ...') is straightforward once the end evidence is attached.\"]"
