  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:6450",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "[\"The stay clause ('shall be stayed until 90 days after the effective date of this code') has its own end at the code's effective date plus 90 days, before the June 14, 1935 repeal; the effective date of the Code of Fair Competition for the Precious Jewelry Producing Industry is not held. The approved code text (III NRA Codes 365, per the WPA list) or an NRA release or other record stating when the code took effect is needed, with its custody, then a corrected inventory of two clauses (the approval; the stay) with the approval ended by the repeal and the stay by its own terms.\", \"The machine inventory is one whole clause (characters 740-1782) that merges the approval and the stay; the corrected inventory must split them. No held source other than the approving order names the Precious Jewelry code (name search of held texts numbered 6200-7100, 2026-10-29), so no earlier cancellation or modification was found.\"]"
  },
  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:6454",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "[\"No held text of EO 6454 (November 27, 1933, Code of Fair Competition for the Warm Air Furnace Manufacturing Industry): the dossier has no original evidence record and no clause inventory, and the override columns need a held original to cite. Needed: a registered text of the order with custody (an APP mirror capture of the page at the URL named in jobs/clark-discovery/output/WEB_NUMBERS_NAMED.csv, a HathiTrust GPO copy or a printed copy), its page check, then a re-prepared packet; only then can the clause inventory, own terms and earlier ends be read.\", \"Until the text is held, whether the order carries conditions, stays or exceptions (like EO 6450 and EO 6606-C of the same period) is unknown, and no earlier-end search can be scoped to its terms. The register and WPA listings identify the order and its date only.\"]"
  },
